  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 221136\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM HST Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on Tropical\nStorm Vance, located several hundred miles south-southwest of\nAcapulco, Mexico.\n\nWestern Central Pacific:\nAn area of low pressure is forecast to form near the International\nDate Line, a few hundred miles west-southwest of Johnston Atoll\nlate this weekend or early next week.  Environmental conditions\nappear conducive for some gradual development thereafter while the\nsystem moves generally eastward to east-northeastward.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.\n\n&&\nPublic advisories on Tropical Storm Vance are issued under WMO\nheader WTPZ32 KNHC and under AWIPS header MIATCPEP2.\nForecast/advisories on Tropical Storm Vance are issued under WMO\nheader WTPZ22 KNHC and under AWIPS header MIATCMEP2.\n\n$$\nForecaster Beven\nNNNN",
